          "verdict": "malicious",
          "reasoning": "On workstation5, PowerShell (proc-cd779cc96d, user wardog) connected out to 151.101.208.133:443 (Fastly CDN, typical of raw GitHub content). At 07:52:05.767 it wrote T1218.005.hta into wardog's Startup folder (file-ba7e4ec7d0). It then started mshta.exe (proc-35906d273e) to run that HTA at High integrity. The HTA started cmd.exe /c calc.exe (proc-2a27e0bff6), which launched conhost and calc.exe (proc-bc2e6841ef). This is mshta proxy execution (T1218.005) plus a Startup-folder autostart, so the HTA runs again at every logon. The pattern matches an Atomic Red Team simulation, but the behavior itself is malicious: a downloaded HTA run by mshta from a persistence location that spawns a shell.",
